- The Hon. Prime Minister brought to the notice of the Cabinet the following programme proposed for the Budget Debate related to the financial year 2023 and the Cabinet granted its concurrence for the said programme.
*	Budget Speech (Second Reading of the Appropriation Bill): 2022‑11‑14;

*	Second Reading Debate (from 2022‑11‑15 to 2022‑11‑22 (07 days);

*	Committee Stage Debate : from 2022‑11‑23 to 2022‑12‑08                 (13 days); and

*	Vote: 2022‑12‑08

- The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the following Gazette Notifications to Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet.

i	Five (05) Gazette Notifications which include the Orders issued under section 2 and section 5 of the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007;

ii	Two (02) Gazette Notifications which include the Orders issued under section 2 of the Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962;

iii	Two (02) Gazette Notifications which include the Orders issued under section 14 of the Sri Lanka Export Development Act, No.40 of 1979;

iv	Two (02) Gazette Notifications which include the Orders issued under section 3 of the Ports and Airports Development Levy Act, No.18 of 2011; and 

v	One (01) Gazette Notification which includes the Orders issued under section 2A of 	the Value Added Tax Act, No.6 of 2005.

- The debris and wreck removal of the MV X-Press Pearl subjected to maritime disaster has been commenced and the said activities are to be completed within 120 days. The following further matters submitted by the Minister of Justice in that regard were noted by the Cabinet: 

*	that, in view of ensuring that no further marine pollution takes place due to the debris removal process, a monitoring committee under the chairmanship of the Director General of the Merchant Shipping Secretariat and comprising the representatives of the relevant institutions has been appointed to monitor the said process; 

*	that, the first installment of compensation has been paid to all aggrieved fishermen; 

*	that, the fishing ban in the Kalutara district has been completely lifted; 

*	that, subsequent to the completion of the debris removal process, the said ban in the Colombo and Gampaha districts will also be lifted; 

*	that, USD 3.7 million has been credited to the Government of Sri Lanka as part of the claims of the Fisheries and Marine Environment Protection Authority and negotiations are being conducted with P&I Club to obtain the rest of the claims; 

*	that, bio samples of sea creatures and other samples have been forwarded to foreign laboratories for analysis;   

*	that, Sparke Helmore Lawyers, Australia provide legal advice pertaining to environmental loss claims.

- The Government of Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka has agreed to sign- 


(i)	the Protocol to the Agreement on the Avoidance of Double Taxation and the Prevention of Fiscal Evasion with respect to Taxes on Income with the Government of the Republic of India;

(ii)	the Agreement on the Avoidance of Double Taxation and the Prevention of Fiscal Evasion with respect to Taxes on Income  with the Government of Republic of Turkey;

(iii) 	the Agreement on the Avoidance of Double Taxation and the 	Prevention of Fiscal Evasion with respect to Taxes on Income  	with the Government of Czech Republic. 

Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to sign the above Agreements and submit the same to Parliament for approval in terms of the provisions of the Inland Revenue Act No. 24 of 2017, was approved by the Cabinet.

- It has been planned to implement the Paddy Purchasing Programme of the Government in the Maha Season 2021/2022 with a view to providing a reasonable price for the harvest of farmers and maintaining buffer stock of paddy. Purchase of paddy harvest will be carried out directly by the Paddy Marketing Board and District Secretaries/Government Agents through the small and medium scale millers. Provisions of Rs 29,805 million  required for purchasing said paddy harvest will be secured through the Government banks. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposals made by the Minister of Agriculture, the Cabinet decided- 

(i)	to purchase paddy by the Paddy Marketing Board at the competitive prices with the Private Sector under the Paddy 	Purchasing Programme of the Government in the Maha Season 2021/2022; 

(ii)	to pay a compensation of Rs. 25/- per kg for  securing the 	income level of  farmers affected by the reduction of paddy 	harvest, if any, during the Maha Season 2021/2022.

- The proposal made by the Minister of Finance to present the following Gazette Notifications which include the Orders published under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007 with a view to stabilizing the market price, providing relief to the consumers and protecting the local agriculture, in Parliament for approval.

(i)	Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2236/66 dated 2021‑07‑18; 

