(iv)	Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2249/3 dated 2021‑10‑11; 

(v)	Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2249/16 dated 2021‑10‑13; 

(vi)	Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2252/9 dated 2021‑11‑02; and

(vii)	Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2252/25 dated 	2021‑11‑02.

-The Project Evaluation Committee of the Ministry of Industries has 	recommended the allocation of land blocks as follows to ten investors 	relating to 10 project proposals, based on the recommendations submitted by 	the Regional Industrial Services Committee.

    • Four project proposals for Buttala Industrial Estate;
    • Two project proposals for Laksha Uyana Industrial Estate;
    • One project proposal each for the Industrial Estates of Nalanda Ellawala, Puttlam, Karandeniya and Bata - Atha;

	Under the proposed projects, the relevant investors are expected to invest 	approximately Rs. 1,144 million and through the same around 555 new direct 	employment opportunities will be created. 

	Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to allocate land 	blocks to the aforesaid ten investors for a period of 35 years, on lease basis, 	was approved by the Cabinet.

- The following proposals made by the Minister of Tourism and Civil Aviation, with a view to recommencing the International Scheduled Airline flight operations at the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport and the Regional Operations of the International Airport in Ratmalana and to develop the said Airports, were granted approval by the Cabinet.

	Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport

*	The waving of the Embarkation Levy of US$ 60 at the Airport  completely, for a period of 02 years;

*	Granting of a discount on charges made for migrant workers who depart the Airport;

*	Offering  of a discount rate for ground handling charges of the Airport;

*	Supplying of fuel for airlines at a concessionary price;

*	Waving-off landing and parking charges of scheduled international airlines for a period of 01 year as a promotional incentive.

Colombo International Airport in Ratmalana 

*	Charging of only 50% from the Embarkation Levy of US$ 60 for a period of 01 year;

*	Supplying of fuel for airlines at a concessionary price;

*	Waving-off landing and parking charges of scheduled international airlines for a period of 01 year as a promotional incentive;

- Approval was granted to appoint a Committee at the Cabinet meeting held on 2019‑12‑19, to make recommendations pertaining to the preparation of a simple and convenient mechanism for collecting the relevant rent without causing difficulties for the lessees who lease out Government lands.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Lands & Land Development, to implement the following proposals submitted by the said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet. 

*	Write-off of the interest of the fine to be charged from the lessees;

*	Providing a concessional period of one year for the lessees to pay arrears of lease;

*	Providing them with the opportunity of paying the annual lease rental by 04 installments; 

*	Granting of a discount of 10% for the lessees who pay their annual rentals before the expiry of the first month of the period of lease;

*	Providing facilities for the payment of lease rentals through the modes like post offices, credit cards, mobile phones etc.

- The proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development in regard to the procurement of fertilizer for Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd. and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company Ltd., as follows, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet.

*	47,700 MT of Urea (Granular) at US$ 268.90 per MT to Agrifert Liven International Trading Pte Limited;

*	15,000 MT of Triple Super Phosphate at US$ 262.74 per MT to Valency International Trading Pte. Ltd.;

*	13,600 MT of Muriate of Potash at US$ 317.25 per MT to Agri Commodities and Finance; and

*	3,060 MT Urea (Prilled) for Ceylon Fertilizer Company Limited  at US$ 285.00 per MT to Agri Commodities and Finance.

- The eradication of poverty in the country has been identified as one of the top priorities of the Government in order to create an inclusive and suitable development under the National Policy Framework of the Government - “Saubagyaye Dakma”. Further, the Development Goals identified in the said National Policy Framework of the Government are consistent with the 17 Sustainable Development Goals of the United Nations. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President to implement the following proposals on priority basis with a view to eradicating the poverty in the country, was approved by the Cabinet.

*	Implementing a programme ensuring the food security of low income families by providing them with essential food items;

*	The programme for providing 100,000 jobs for 100,000 poor families;

*	Implementing the programme for providing the poor families with houses under the programme of “One House - One Village” on an accelerated basis;

*	Implementing the rural road development programme of 100,000 km to provide quality road access facilities for at least 1,000,000 households; and

*	Providing easy access to credit prioritizing the small business development, self-employment and household needs and household level livelihood development  initiatives.

- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019 10 29 had granted approval to sign a compact Agreement and a Programme Implementation Agreement between the Millennium Challenge Corporation of the USA and the Government of Sri Lanka to obtain the grant funds provided by the Office of the Millennium Challenge Corporation for the implementation of several programmes of the identified fields. However, taking into consideration the views expressed on the project by various parties, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister to appoint a Committee comprising of the following to make a comprehensive study on the Millennium Challenge Corporation Project and submit recommendations to the Government and to suspend taking action in terms of  the Cabinet decision dated 2019 10 29 in this respect, until such time that the Committee makes its recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet.

*	Prof. Lalithasiri Gunaruwan - (Chairman);

*	Mr. D.S. Jayaweera,
	former Secretary to the Ministry of Transport;

*	Mr. Nihal Jayawardena P.C.; and

*	Mr. Nalaka Jayaweera.

- The proposal made by H.E. the President to appoint the Cabinet Sub Committee on Cost of Living under the Chairmanship of H.E. the President comprising the following members to make recommendations to the Cabinet regarding the matters concerning the cost of living, was approved by the Cabinet.

*	Hon. the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development;

*	The Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development and the Minister of Internal Trade, Food Security and Consumer Welfare;

*	The Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources; and

*	The Minister of Plantation Industries and Export Agriculture

It was also decided to appoint a Committee comprising of 06 State Ministers and 12 Officials to assist the said Sub Committee.
